{"game_id":2026020108,"away":"BUF","home":"TOR","split":{"name":"McKenna","side":1,"sec":1820},"lede":"Toronto had last change, so Jim Hiller picked most of these matchups. Toronto played without Bo Groulx and Chris Tanev and lost Gavin McKenna after 10:20 of the second. Buffalo played without Rasmus Dahlin and Jiří Kulich.","notes":[{"kind":"swing","head":"One matchup paid off","text":"Roslovic, Matthews and Nylander kept drawing Buffalo’s second line, Thompson, McLeod and Doan. In those 5:41 Toronto had 0.89 expected goals to Buffalo’s 0.31. Toronto scored one of its four goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After McKenna left, the lines changed","text":"Duhaime moved up beside Sissons and Cowan (3:32 together). Blueger went from 20% to 30% and Roslovic from 27% to 36% of Toronto’s 5-on-5 time, and Tavares dropped from 27% to 10%. The matchups changed: Nylander’s line against Buffalo’s second line (50% before, 21% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went worse","text":"Toronto had 1.63 to 0.92 expected goals at 5-on-5 before McKenna left and 0.81 to 0.85 after. The third line went from 0.39 to 0.28 with McKenna to 0.20 to 0.10 with Duhaime. Toronto led for most of that stretch, though, and a team ahead usually sits back, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Jim Hiller matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 42% of its time against one opposing line, against 39% to 41% in his first four.","periods":{"all":{"0":{"rows":[{"label":"L1","names":["Benson","Östlund","Quinn"],"sec":980,"mixed":45,"vs":[414,194,258,114],"xgf":0.8,"xga":0.61,"gf":3,"ga":0,"cells":[[0.33,0.22,0,0],[0.18,0.0,1,0],[0.24,0.05,2,0],[0.03,0.17,0,0]]},{"label":"L2","names":["Thompson","McLeod","Doan"],"sec":958,"mixed":15,"vs":[341,204,225,188],"xgf":0.5,"xga":1.1,"gf":1,"ga":1,"cells":[[0.31,0.89,1,1],[0.04,0.14,0,0],[0.13,0.06,0,0],[0.02,0.02,0,0]]},{"label":"L3","names":["Krebs","Norris","Helenius"],"sec":734,"mixed":14,"vs":[98,426,120,90],"xgf":0.37,"xg